<body class="article">
<div id="header">
<h1>Set the Safe Mode Using the API</h1>
</div>
<div id="content">
<div id="preamble">
<div class="sectionbody">
<div class="paragraph">
<p>When using Asciidoctor via the API, the default <a href="ROOT:safe-modes.html">safe mode</a> is <code>SECURE</code>.
You can change the safe mode using the <code>:safe</code> API option.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="sect1">
<h2 id="_set_safe_option">Set :safe option</h2>
<div class="sectionbody">
<div class="paragraph">
<p>The safe mode can be controlled from the API using the <code>:safe</code> option.
The <code>:safe</code> option is accepted by all <a href="index.html#entrypoints">entrypoint methods</a> (e.g., <code>Asciidoctor#convert_file</code>).</p>
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
<p>The <code>:safe</code> option accepts the safe mode as a string:</p>
</div>
<div class="listingblock">
<div class="content">
<pre class="highlight"><code class="language-ruby" data-lang="ruby">Asciidoctor.convert_file 'doc.adoc', safe: 'server'</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
<p>as a symbol (preferred):</p>
</div>
<div class="listingblock">
<div class="content">
<pre class="highlight"><code class="language-ruby" data-lang="ruby">Asciidoctor.convert_file 'doc.adoc', safe: :server</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
<p>as an integer:</p>
</div>
<div class="listingblock">
<div class="content">
<pre class="highlight"><code class="language-ruby" data-lang="ruby">Asciidoctor.convert_file 'doc.adoc', safe: 10</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
<p>You can also set the <a href="cli:set-safe-mode.html">safe mode from the CLI</a> and <a href="ROOT:reference-safe-mode.html">enable or disable content based on the current safe mode</a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
